{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs4JHcWz2m7cLn6hvKFm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`wc` now has a `--json` flag. The test suite passes (5 tests, including 4 new ones), and text output is byte-identical to the original.\n\n**Changes** (uncommitted, in `wc/cli.py` and `tests/test_cli.py`):\n\n- **`wc/cli.py`**: Added `--json` as a `store_true` option. In JSON mode the per-file table lines are suppressed, successful files are collected, and one object is printed at the end: `{\"files\": [...], \"total\": {...}}`. Each entry in `files` is `{\"path\", \"lines\", \"words\", \"chars\"}` in that key order.\n- **Missing files**: The error still goes to stderr and the exit code is 1 in both modes. In JSON mode the missing file is left out of `files`, and `total` counts only the files that were read.\n- **Text mode**: Same code path as before. The text-mode total line still appears only when more than one file is given.\n\n**Tests added:**\n- `test_text_missing_file`: text-mode error and exit code, with output checked.\n- `test_json`: single file.\n- `test_json_multiple_files`: multiple files, with totals summed.\n- `test_json_missing_file`: missing file excluded from `files`, error on stderr, exit 1.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `python -m pytest -q` gives 5 passed.\n- I ran the original code (from `git archive HEAD`) and the new code on the same inputs: one file, two copies of the same file, a file plus a missing file, and a missing file alone. Stdout, stderr, and exit codes matched in every case.\n\n**Decisions I made:**\n- `total` is always present in JSON mode, including for a single file.\n- Multiple missing files are reported one by one on stderr, as before, and each is omitted from `files`.\n\nI removed the `__pycache__` directories my test runs created and did not commit."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3443,"cache_read_input_tokens":36804,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3443},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d75c6ef-4be4-4c0f-afcf-408a8429018c","uuid":"ecd91b52-719a-4e6d-a45a-90e537800e9d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:28:25.379Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs4JHLtg1BhGdAbSBSwp"}
